{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do","id":1074062,"title":"GMing Demon: What NOT to do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-06T02:17:13-07:00","id":1074062,"title":"GMing Demon: What NOT to do?","content":"As the title somewhat implies, I've had some interest in running a game of Demon in the future. Having played a number of games with different GMs and players, I can safely say it has a number of hurtles that the GM needs to avoid. Demon is complicated, with the plots, the counter plots, characters, infrastructure and happenstance that needs to all come together without making the experience a mire to get through. Though mistakes will inevitably happen, I'd like to preemptively learn how to avoid the worst and be properly prepared. Failure can teach as much as (if not more than) success, but I've also learned from experience it's best to have a good platform to start from to make sure that one egregious failure doesn't stop future attempts.<br /> <br /> What advice do you all, either as players or GMs yourselves, have to avoiding particular pitfalls? What plots should not be done and characters should not be evoked, and how do you keep the group working together when they have very different characters with differing ideologies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-06-2017, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T13:10:20-07:00","id":1074287,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>The game pitch comes before the characters. Get your players together and formulate an idea of what the game will be about, what kind of ring will suit it, and why the ring is working together <i>before</i> your players start coming up with characters, so that they cohere and you don't have to stretch yourself thin incorporating them. This is advice that cross-applies to games in general.</li> <li>Don't nitpick with compromise risks. The consequences of a compromise are significant enough that they build tension well as rare and dangerous moments rather than an ever-present annoyance. A demon has some leeway in breaking the character of a Cover. It's only <i>gross</i> contradictions that directly risk compromise.</li> <li>Don't undermine achievements. There's a valid atmosphere of paranoia to build in how much the God-Machine is really ahead of the ring, but making things too explicit can drain agency. Occult matrices depend upon myriad background factors that only coincide once in a blue moon, meaning that if a project is disrupted before it can fire, it's not a simple matter for the God-Machine to simply &quot;try again&quot; somewhere else.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T22:11:55-07:00","id":1074999,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> (wow that feels weird to write), those are all great points. The first one is something that I've run afoul of before, where there wasn't really a game pitch, more of a sandbox the characters were plopped down into with some plot added in after the dust settled. It has merit, but in my case it made the characters very disparate and coordination between them very hit and miss. It didn't help that half of those games were also ones where other players deliberately kept their characters separate from the other players' in the conception stage, which made it hard to figure out how they were supposed to work together and their covers fit in with one another.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that Demons are supposed to be suspicious of one another, and keeping characters separate before, during or even after character creation means that players aren't meta-gaming, but I find it more frustrating than anything else. Again, it has merit, it just wasn't something that worked for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:05:47-07:00","id":1075108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do#post1074062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What advice do you all, either as players or GMs yourselves, have to avoiding particular pitfalls? What plots should not be done and characters should not be evoked, and how do you keep the group working together when they have very different characters with differing ideologies?</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to making demons work together the answer is simple. They have a common enemy and sharing intelligence, and sometimes pulling off daring heists and the like, is one of their best protections and weapons against It, More paranoid and less likeable demons do this on a purely transactional basis, but nicer ones may do it out of the goodness of their metal hearts, or to build alliances and friendships. Integrators can be harder to fit into this paradigm, though I've yet to see a player playing as an actual 'I will betray you to the Machine' Turncoat. heck, some Integrators (those of the 'the Machine needs fixing' philosophy) might even to play well with Saboteurs.<br /> <br /> A big part of fostering this is building your setting. If you're starting as freshly Fallen, newbies demons, Special Message might be useful for a demon who acts as a local 'welcoming committee' to introduce you to local Unchained politics. Agencies might want recruits. My own demon settings generally have demons falling into discrete roles in an Unchained society - information brokers, Cover and Pact-suppliers, extradimensional real-estate experts (ie, boltholes and Splintes), Infrastructure- archaeologists, bespoke Gadgeteers, smugglers, spies-for-hire, muscle for hire, demonic cryptozoologists... Players might speak to, or hire, these experts or be hired in turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 04-14-2017, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T18:17:25-07:00","id":1075659,"title":"","content":"<b>EDIT:</b> Was thinking of Demon: the Fallen. Please Ignore!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2017, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:01:17-07:00","id":1077670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do?p=1075108#post1075108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you're starting as freshly Fallen, newbies demons, Special Message might be useful for a demon who acts as a local 'welcoming committee' to introduce you to local Unchained politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god this was the simplest-and-yet-the-best idea I read for putting characters together and developing so many plot hooks ! Thank you so much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You may have a cookie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5690-mithrael","name":"Mithrael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:31:22-07:00","id":1077850,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar452_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"452\" data-vbnamecard=\"452\">Eremite</a> As per usual, you are great to read from on the matter of Demon. I hadn't actually thought on using Special Message like that before, but it makes total sense to; now I'm going to look into what other Embeds could allow discrete instruction and or obfuscation. It was actually from your very post I got the idea on the direction to go with my Demon in my most recent game, a gadgeteer, when before I'd been struggling on a focus. Of course, I had planned on making a number of gadgets to begin with, since I find them very fun (though the effective one experience cost is a bit prohibitive), but making it the character's focus/specialization wasn't something I had thought on before. It's something I'll want to ponder on for future games too. Thank you for the awesome advice~<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> It's all good! Thanks for posting all the same, even if it was for a different gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T03:25:02-07:00","id":1078254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do?p=1075108#post1075108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When it comes to making demons, a paranoid bunch, the answer is simple. They have a common enemy and sharing intelligence, and sometimes pulling off daring heists and the like, is one of their best protections and weapons against It, More paranoid and less likeable demons do this on a purely transactional basis, but nicer ones may do it out of the goodness of their metal hearts, or to build alliances and friendships. Integrators can be harder to fit into this paradigm, though I've yet to see a player playing as an actual 'I will betray you to the Machine' Turncoat. heck, some Integrators (those of the 'the Machine needs fixing' philosophy) might even to play well with Saboteurs.<br /> <br /> A big part of fostering this is building your setting. If you're starting as freshly Fallen, newbies demons, Special Message might be useful for a demon who acts as a local 'welcoming committee' to introduce you to local Unchained politics. Agencies might want recruits. My own demon settings generally have demons falling into discrete roles in an Unchained society - information brokers, Cover and Pact-suppliers, extradimensional real-estate expert (ie, boltholes and Splintes), Infrastructure- archaeologists, bespoke Gadgeteers, smugglers, spies-for-hire, muscle for hire, demonic cryptozoologists... Players might speak to, or hire, these experts or be hired in turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my gosh this was so helpful! And I am so glad that Special Message has a good purpose for just this sorta thing. I actually did this myself with a player recently and I felt so sure that I was actually just grasping at straws that that Special Messaging a recently Fallen was actually just like, deus ex machina or too silly for words. I feel so much better now!<br /> <br /> More importantly, this makes making the background characters of Unchained a lot less daunting, thank you so much! Also might I just say that the Demon Dark Era's stole the books, they were my favorites!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T20:50:18-07:00","id":1080728,"title":"","content":"I have some advice based on personal experience: moderate the paranoia of your players. While some paranoia is good and encouraged for the game, having too much will cause nothing to get done because everyone's too scared to take anything on at a low level of Primum. There was a game I was in where half the players had played with the GM previously, and knew they could be devious and extremely dangerous, and they were open about that concern. Consequently, near everything close to a plothook was viewed as a deathtrap, which meant our progress was slow and all over the place; I imagine the GM was frustrated when so many of their carefully made infrastructure was either passed over or mis-attributed for being more deadly than it was.<br /> <br /> The ironic thing is that the GM wasn't doing it intentionally; in fact, they said that the paranoia level they were going for was a 1 out of 10.<br /> <br /> I guess another way to put it is to make sure players are paranoid of the game, not the person running it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-19-2017, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T15:26:01-08:00","id":1182091,"title":"","content":"Upon reflection of the games I've been in, I have another bit of advice. If you have starting Demons who have barely bought anything with experiences, don't set them up with something that is out of their range when they seize upon an opportunity to infiltrate Infrastructure. Sure, Infrastructure isn't usually that easy to hack into, but if they get in at least make sure they can actually do something about it or at least learn from it. If you don't, you're going to leave them frustrated and having left evidence of their infiltration, meaning that the next chance they get (should they get one) will be even harder.<br /> <br /> Edit: I decided to delete my second point from this. After speaking with the ST of that game, I realized that a lot of that was simply annoyance from another issue and, in spite of not naming names, came off as talking behind someone's back. Further examining what I posted also showed that it wasn't a bad idea in and of itself, given that even in-game the God-Machine has backups for such a scenario. Just a bad reaction from me.<br /> <br /> I keep my point about the Infrastructure though; be mindful of what a player character can handle before you set up a challenge for them. That initial annoyance will go a long way in a player's memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 02-05-2018, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T19:46:27-08:00","id":1182782,"title":"","content":"I think probably the biggest difficulty Demon faces is that the game naturally inclines you to avoid going on adventures etc; demons are primarily focused on their first Covers, but nearly anything they do will typically serve to fray their Cover, and most missions don't directly relate to improving it. Similarly, demons usually only risk exposure to the extent that they perform actions, and are rewarded for staying totally in character with their Cover. The default tone of the game is to flee, hide, or oppose the God Machine, but nearly anything they do to oppose it will make it devote more resources, or have an easier time, at finding them.<br /> <br /> As a result, if PCs are supposed to combat the God Machine, I suggest having their Agencies, or other NPCs trying to get them to act, to give pretty hefty rewards that exceed what they will have to expend for victory. Otherwise, I expect that in many cases, the fact that play time means Covers will fray and getting patch jobs are more of an intimate 1 on 1 affair can result in the PCs being better off avoiding story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T19:58:54-08:00","id":1182784,"title":"","content":"Worth remembering that Cover is not a precious treasure to be kept-it's a resource to be spent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T03:19:15-08:00","id":1182853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do?p=1182784#post1182784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth remembering that Cover is not a precious treasure to be kept-it's a resource to be spent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it is a Cover the Demon is particularly attached to. In that case it's &quot;No, you can't touch my mint condition [collectible]. Use these other toys - this is <i>mine</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T03:27:45-08:00","id":1182856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do?p=1182782#post1182782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think probably the biggest difficulty Demon faces is that the game naturally inclines you to avoid going on adventures etc; demons are primarily focused on their first Covers, but nearly anything they do will typically serve to fray their Cover, and most missions don't directly relate to improving it. Similarly, demons usually only risk exposure to the extent that they perform actions, and are rewarded for staying totally in character with their Cover. The default tone of the game is to flee, hide, or oppose the God Machine, but nearly anything they do to oppose it will make it devote more resources, or have an easier time, at finding them.<br /> <br /> As a result, if PCs are supposed to combat the God Machine, I suggest having their Agencies, or other NPCs trying to get them to act, to give pretty hefty rewards that exceed what they will have to expend for victory. Otherwise, I expect that in many cases, the fact that play time means Covers will fray and getting patch jobs are more of an intimate 1 on 1 affair can result in the PCs being better off avoiding story hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also have the Plot incidentally involve said-Demons' Covers: If the G-M's next Occult Matrix is going to require your Cover's best friend/sister/[other important NPC] to be sacrifices, the Demon <i>needs</i> to oppose it or their Cover is going to degrade <i>anyways</i>.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Aspirations are A Thing. Dangle the satisfaction of the Demon/Player's goals there - it's a Storyteller's job to make sure the reward outweighs the risk enough to get PCs to act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T17:37:17-08:00","id":1183105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do?p=1182853#post1182853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless it is a Cover the Demon is particularly attached to. In that case it's &quot;No, you can't touch my mint condition [collectible]. Use these other toys - this is <i>mine</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact a lot of players like hoarding resources and can be a bit risk-averse so they need a nudge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T10:45:09-08:00","id":1183303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do?p=1182856#post1182856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Additionally, Aspirations are A Thing. Dangle the satisfaction of the Demon/Player's goals there - it's a Storyteller's job to make sure the reward outweighs the risk enough to get PCs to act.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is particularly good advice. Demon, more than other games, can have the PCs suffer from paranoia; it's a core theme after all. Listen to what your players want and use those desires to get them to engage with the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T11:23:14-08:00","id":1184021,"title":"","content":"I agree completely on not undermining achievements. If they are able to stop an Occult Matrix from reaching completion or shut down an established piece of Infrastructure, those are feats worth rewarding and praising in game.<br /> <br /> At the same time, in my experience it is also paramount that you make it explicitly clear that the players cannot gain a permanent or lasting Advantage or victory against the Machine. They are fighting a guerilla war against an entity that outclasses them by orders of magnitude upon orders of magnitude, and they will never be as remotely powerful as It is. They can only inconvenience the Machine, but those inconveniences are still incredibly impressive victories.<br /> <br /> In short, let them grow, but don\u2019t be afraid to knock them down a peg or three if they get delusions of grandeur.<br /> <br /> It is a game of espionage against an entire world spanning Machine who\u2019s agents are everywhere and they are far better equipped than you are after all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 02-09-2018, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-14T16:36:47-07:00","id":1260586,"title":"","content":"If your players buys the Cultists merit, don't make the characters who are becoming said cultists deliberately annoying, dismissive and or disbelieving of their new leader(s). This goes double for if the players have gone to significant lengths to help these characters before or during this period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T03:41:48-07:00","id":1261075,"title":"","content":"Also, and this is extremely important, do not let the players become angel slaying demigods. Unless it\u2019s rank 1, or they have its Ban or Bane, you want your angels to be highly dangerous, challenging opponents that impresses upon the Ring that it\u2019s probably a good idea to retreat and regroup rather than fight, only fighting an angel when there is no other choice. <br /> <br /> This is what god-machine cultists and the odd Cryptid is for, if you want prolonged fire fights","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 10-17-2018, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T10:02:02-07:00","id":1261130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do?p=1261075#post1261075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, and this is extremely important, do not let the players become angel slaying demigods. Unless it\u2019s rank 1, or they have its Ban or Bane, you want your angels to be highly dangerous, challenging opponents that impresses upon the Ring that it\u2019s probably a good idea to retreat and regroup rather than fight, only fighting an angel when there is no other choice. <br /> <br /> This is what god-machine cultists and the odd Cryptid is for, if you want prolonged fire fights</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it is a long-running Chronicle with Sabotuers and they <i>want</i> to become angel-slaying demi-gods and have been putting the effort towards it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T11:05:25-07:00","id":1261139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do?p=1261130#post1261130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless it is a long-running Chronicle with Sabotuers and they <i>want</i> to become angel-slaying demi-gods and have been putting the effort towards it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s end game stuff then, because they will have to work hard every step of the way in my opinion \ud83d\ude06","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T19:53:55-07:00","id":1261226,"title":"","content":"Something I've noticed lately is that people forget angels and demons are BIO-mechanical. Remember that not everything is pure robotics, there are just as many angels and demons that are organic or a freakish fusion of both","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-17T21:50:18-07:00","id":1261239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1074062-gming-demon-what-not-to-do?p=1261226#post1261226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've noticed lately is that people forget angels and demons are BIO-mechanical. Remember that not everything is pure robotics, there are just as many angels and demons that are organic or a freakish fusion of both</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the long fight, it doesn't end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud8